  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Hero Section**\n\nOkay, I\'m focusing on the single-file, scroll-driven hero section for NORVA. I\'ve decided on plain HTML, CSS, and vanilla JS. No frameworks, no build step. I\'m visualizing the core layout first, aiming for a clean, impactful design that highlights the company\'s identity. I am now exploring potential animations triggered by scrolling.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Target Environment**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the environment. I need to figure out how to best integrate the HTML, CSS, and vanilla JS. I\'ve realized it\'s an Android context, with files like `build.gradle.kts`. The original user prompt requested a \"local host\" setup, but now I\'m thinking about hosting within a WebView or local server within the Android app, or maybe serving or providing both of these options or a WebView in Compose with local HTML assets. I am also circling back to understand the user\'s intent.\n\n\n"
