  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Confirming Setup Availability**\n\nOkay, I\'ve confirmed that `python3` and `node` are accessible. I\'ve also verified that, within the streaming emulator on Android, the application is visible and launches successfully. Specifically, the Android app\'s APK is installed and the app runs in the emulator. Now, I\'m focusing on the full-screen modern WebView and its local content.\n\n\n**Analyzing Landing Page Design**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the single-file landing page. I\'m focusing on the NORVA brand and the 3D isometric miniature design. I\'m carefully evaluating how to implement this visually and functionally, ensuring smooth rendering within the Android WebView, and making sure all requirements are met.\n\n\n**Integrating City Visualization**\n\nI\'m now focused on incorporating the provided visual assets. The plan is to seamlessly integrate the city scene\342\200\224graphite buildings, glowing elements, and route lines\342\200\224into the landing page. My current thoughts are on the smooth camera motion via the glide clips, with a focus on their specifications for optimal playback and responsiveness on various screen sizes. I am particularly concerned with a seamless transition to the four-step process list after the camera\'s glide over the cityscape, ensuring a cohesive user experience.\n\n\n**Defining Typography and Colour**\n\nI\'m now establishing the typography and colour palette. I intend to use Inter Tight for the font, either through Google Fonts or self-hosting, with specified weights, sizes, and tracking for headlines, body text, and UI labels. I will be incorporating the provided colours, including night, ink, pill grey, lime, cyan, and using rgba for various alpha levels. Also, I\'m defining a custom unit \"u\" to maintain visual consistency across different screen sizes.\n\n\n**Designing Navigation and Copy**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the landing page\'s content arrangement, particularly the navigation and hero copy. I\'ve worked on setting up a fixed navigation bar, 58u tall, with three columns. It includes the \"NORVA\" wordmark in the center, and the \"OUR INDUSTRIES\" and \"OUR MISSION\" links on the left, and the \"APPLY\" and \"REQUEST CREWS\" buttons on the right. Currently, I\'m working on the hero section placement, ensuring the text is properly formatted within a `perspective: 900u` stage. This is followed by considerations of the scroll cue and the initial inactive state of the process list, detailing the visual aspects and interaction.\n\n\n**Implementing Process Sections**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the four process rows and the scroll behavior. I\'ve defined the content for each row, including headlines and descriptions, and am working on styling the background scenes. I\'m also planning the scroll behavior, which will involve a sticky scene with a video and a progress-based clip for the seamless arrival. I am also working on light shading.\n\n\n**Refining Scroll Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now implementing the scroll behavior tied to video playback within the application. I\'m focusing on smooth transitions, using a requestAnimationFrame loop with a target-based interpolation, considering `currentTime` updates, and seeking only when necessary. The UI elements, including headlines and the process list, are being defined as pure functions of the playback progress, ensuring synchronized visual changes with scrolling. The goal is a responsive and fluid user experience.\n\n\n**Defining Loader Animations**\n\nI\'m now implementing the loader animations. I\'ve designed a full-screen night panel with two dotted ellipses and a spinning mark composed of cyan squares and a lime chevron. I\'m ensuring the loader fades out after a specified duration based on clip loading, and that it has an alternative animation for reduced motion preferences. Additionally, I\'m working on the recorder mode functionality, which allows for a controlled playback sequence and specific timing.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Landing Page Content**\n\nI\'m now implementing the final content styling. I\'m finalizing the typographic scales: headlines are (38px, 11vw, 48px), sublines (15px, up to 34ch), and the process list (full width, 18px gutters, 22px from the bottom). I\'ve ensured there is no sideways scroll. Finally, I\'m checking the acceptance criteria. On load, the loader fades to the night city. As the user scrolls, the headline and camera movements are as specified: step 01, cyan routes to glowing hub, step 02, etc. I\'ve also confirmed that there are no external logos. The landing page is now ready and open in local host. I\'ve also confirmed that `metadata.json`, `strings.xml`, `settings.gradle.kts` and `app/build.gradle.kts` are correct.\n\n\n**Generating App Icon**\n\nI\'m now focusing on generating the custom adaptive launcher icon. I\'m checking the `generate_image` tool and considering using ImageMagick if necessary, following the specifications from the `app-icon-generation` skill. I\'ll use the `#0f1626` hex color for the background. I\'ll then move on to integrating the necessary configurations for the Android app manifest, assets, and `MainActivity` to ensure the WebView loads the landing page from local assets and connects to either CloudFront or a local fallback. Finally, I\'ll ensure a localhost HTTP server runs at port 8080.\n\n\n"
